{
  "mark.11.p1.b1": {
    "text": "As they approached Jerusalem and came to Bethphage and Bethany at the Mount of Olives,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:1"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p1.b2": {
    "text": "Go into the village ahead of you, and as soon as you enter it, you will find a colt tied there,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:2"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p1.b3": {
    "text": "On which no one has ever sat. Untie it and bring it here.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:2"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p1.b4": {
    "text": "If anyone asks, ‘Why are you doing this?’ tell him, ‘The Lord needs it",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:3"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p2.b1": {
    "text": "So they went and found the colt outside in the street, tied at a doorway.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:4"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p2.b2": {
    "text": "Why are you untying the colt?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:5"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p2.b3": {
    "text": "The disciples answered as Jesus had instructed them, and the people gave them permission.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:6"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p3.b1": {
    "text": "Then they led the colt to Jesus and threw their cloaks over it, and He sat on it.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:7"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p3.b2": {
    "text": "Many in the crowd spread their cloaks on the road, while others spread branches they had cut from the fields.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:8"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p4.b1": {
    "text": "Hosanna!",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:9"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p4.b2": {
    "text": "Blessed is He who comes in the name of the Lord!",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:9"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p4.b3": {
    "text": "Blessed is the coming kingdom of our father David!",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:10"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p4.b4": {
    "text": "Hosanna in the highest!",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:10"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p5.b1": {
    "text": "Then Jesus entered Jerusalem and went into the temple courts.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:11"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p5.b2": {
    "text": "He looked around at everything,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:11"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p5.b3": {
    "text": "Since it was already late, He went out to Bethany with the Twelve.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:11"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p6.b1": {
    "text": "The next day, when they had left Bethany, Jesus was hungry.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:12"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p6.b2": {
    "text": "Seeing in the distance a fig tree in leaf, He went to see if there was any fruit on it.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:13"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p6.b3": {
    "text": "But when He reached it, He found nothing on it except leaves, since it was not the season for figs.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:13"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p6.b4": {
    "text": "May no one ever eat of your fruit again.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:14"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p7.b1": {
    "text": "When they arrived in Jerusalem, Jesus entered the temple courts",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:15"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p7.b2": {
    "text": "And began to drive out those who were buying and selling there.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:15"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p7.b3": {
    "text": "He overturned the tables of the money changers and the seats of those selling doves.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:15"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p8.b1": {
    "text": "And He would not allow anyone to carry merchandise through the temple courts.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:16"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p8.b2": {
    "text": "Is it not written: ‘My house will be called a house of prayer for all the nations’?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:17"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p8.b3": {
    "text": "But you have made it ‘a den of robbers.’",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:17"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p9.b1": {
    "text": "When the chief priests and scribes heard this, they looked for a way to kill Him.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:18"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p9.b2": {
    "text": "For they were afraid of Him, because the whole crowd was astonished at His teaching.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:18"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p9.b3": {
    "text": "And when evening came, Jesus and His disciples went out of the city.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:19"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p10.b1": {
    "text": "As they were walking back in the morning,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:20"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p10.b2": {
    "text": "They saw the fig tree withered from its roots.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:20"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p10.b3": {
    "text": "Look, Rabbi!",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:21"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p10.b4": {
    "text": "The fig tree You cursed has withered.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:21"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p11.b1": {
    "text": "Have faith in God,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:22"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p11.b2": {
    "text": "Truly I tell you that if anyone says to this mountain, ‘Be lifted up and thrown into the sea,’",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:23"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p11.b3": {
    "text": "And has no doubt in his heart but believes that it will happen, it will be done for him.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:23"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p12.b1": {
    "text": "Therefore I tell you, whatever you ask for in prayer, believe that you have received it, and it will be yours.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:24"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p12.b2": {
    "text": "And when you stand to pray, if you hold anything against another, forgive it,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:25"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p12.b3": {
    "text": "So that your Father in heaven will forgive your trespasses as well.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:25"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p13.b1": {
    "text": "After their return to Jerusalem,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:27"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p13.b2": {
    "text": "Jesus was walking in the temple courts, and the chief priests, scribes, and elders came up to Him.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:27"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p13.b3": {
    "text": "By what authority are You doing these things?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:28"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p13.b4": {
    "text": "And who gave You the authority to do them?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:28"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p14.b1": {
    "text": "I will ask you one question, … and if you answer Me,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:29"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p14.b2": {
    "text": "I will tell you by what authority I am doing these things.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:29"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p14.b3": {
    "text": "John’s baptism—was it from heaven or from men?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:30"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p14.b4": {
    "text": "Answer Me!",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:30"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p15.b1": {
    "text": "If we say, ‘From heaven,’",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:31"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p15.b2": {
    "text": "He will ask, ‘Why then did you not believe him?’",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:31"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p15.b3": {
    "text": "But if we say, ‘From men’... they were afraid of the people,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:32"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p15.b4": {
    "text": "For they all held that John truly was a prophet.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:32"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p16.b1": {
    "text": "We do not know.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:33"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.11.p16.b2": {
    "text": "Neither will I tell you by what authority I am doing these things.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 11:33"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  }
}
